title.narrative:
1.3.3. Regional interlocutors (EuroMed Rights):
# of interactions and spaces/platforms where youth are prepared or included in dialogues and actively participate in joint actions and advocacy ; 
Evidence of joint actions and advocacy across the regions (MENA and Europe); Examples of the concrete actions on HR issues as a result of the joint dialogues

target.value:
1. 0 CEDAW or UPR recommendations of 2022 align with the contents of the reforms 
2. Some recognition amongst DBs that young people’s SRH is important; 
3. Law 103-13 regarding violence against women contains gaps and is not implemented; 
4. Limited mobilization and organizing for increased political representation among youth and WHROs; 
5. Need for increased capacity to identify, address and analyse gender norms and gender stereotypes critically
